From 37c7784671c6d05fae745a4311b2d47f5f21906d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 06:25:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Gate 2 prep: OpenRouter provider smoke test + NeuraBash
 literacy check driver

No provider code changes needed -- OpenRouter already works through the
existing openai-completions adapter (getModel("openrouter", ...) resolves
the fixed target model with the exact required baseUrl; OPENROUTER_API_KEY
is already the mapped env var; ModelRegistry needs no special-casing).

Two standalone driver scripts, same non-CLI-flag pattern as the existing
run-neura-session.ts (baseToolsOverride takes real AgentTool instances,
which don't fit Prime's string/boolean CLI args):

- gate2-provider-smoke-test.ts: proves auth/fixed-model/streaming/real
  tool-call-and-result work end to end against a live (non-faux) model,
  via the "rlm" host tool from the reachability spike. PASS.
- gate2-neurabash-literacy-check.ts: has the fixed model generate 4 tiny
  |!> commands from the real (not aspirational) NeuraBash op surface, runs
  them unmodified against the real binary. This run came back INVALID --
  the depot's attestation manifest is stale relative to its own compiled
  cache (~16 min gap, NeuraBash's working tree is mid-edit) -- not a model
  or Prime defect. Full writeup in Project NIRA's
  NIRA_PRIME_GATE2_PROVIDER_REPORT.md / _PREREGISTRATION.md.

Gate 2 itself did not run: blocked on NeuraBash's runtime state and on
Matt's explicit approval, per the pre-registered run conditions.

